US English speaker learning Mexican Spanish, A1, saying what they and others do on a weekday ("trabajo", "estudias", "cocina"). The tip is the present-tense endings of regular -ar verbs, so a pattern table shows one -ar verb for yo, tú, él/ella/usted, nosotros and ustedes/ellos, and has the learner complete another -ar verb; Mexican Spanish uses "ustedes", so no vosotros row. Each blank's right ending is the longest choice its answer ends with.